      "text": "The bug is that `compute_minimum_eigenvalue` is given `H`, which is a `QuantumCircuit`. QAOA's cost operator has to be an opflow `OperatorBase`.\n\nThe fix converts the circuit into an operator and passes that instead:\n- `Operator(H)` turns the circuit into its matrix, which is Z⊗Z⊗Z⊗Z here.\n- `SparsePauliOp.from_operator` rewrites that matrix as Pauli terms.\n- `PauliSumOp` wraps the result as the opflow operator QAOA expects.\n\nThe mixer stays as the circuit `H`, because QAOA does accept a `QuantumCircuit` there.\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom qiskit import BasicAer, QuantumCircuit\nfrom qiskit.algorithms import QAOA\nfrom qiskit.algorithms.optimizers import COBYLA\n# FIX: missing conversion tools -> imported PauliSumOp, Operator and SparsePauliOp, because the circuit must be turned into an OperatorBase\nfrom qiskit.opflow import PauliSumOp\nfrom qiskit.quantum_info import Operator, SparsePauliOp\n\nnqubits = 4\nH = QuantumCircuit(nqubits)\nfor i in range(nqubits):\n    H.z(i)\n\nqaoa = QAOA(optimizer=COBYLA(), reps=1, mixer=H,\n            initial_point=np.array([1.0]),\n            quantum_instance=BasicAer.get_backend('statevector_simulator'))\n\n# FIX: passed a QuantumCircuit as the cost operator -> converted H to a PauliSumOp, because compute_minimum_eigenvalue requires an OperatorBase observable\nH_op = PauliSumOp(SparsePauliOp.from_operator(Operator(H)))\nprint(qaoa.compute_minimum_eigenvalue(H_op))\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
